1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,469
Your ice cube never sinks

2
00:00:01,469 --> 00:00:02,775
even though it's solid water!

3
00:00:02,775 --> 00:00:03,254
Why?

4
00:00:03,454 --> 00:00:04,550
When most things freeze

5
00:00:04,550 --> 00:00:06,548
their molecules pack tight, and sink

6
00:00:06,548 --> 00:00:07,833
Water does the opposite

7
00:00:08,033 --> 00:00:09,773
Liquid water molecules are crowded

8
00:00:09,773 --> 00:00:11,678
Freezing locks them with hydrogen bonds

9
00:00:11,678 --> 00:00:13,162
into a six-sided lattice

10
00:00:13,162 --> 00:00:14,250
full of empty gaps

11
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:16,357
So ice grows about 9% bigger

12
00:00:16,357 --> 00:00:17,892
Same weight, bigger volume

13
00:00:17,892 --> 00:00:19,151
so it floats on water

14
00:00:19,351 --> 00:00:21,020
In winter, lakes freeze on top

15
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:22,435
and fish live on underneath

16
00:00:22,635 --> 00:00:24,208
Tiny gaps inside the ice

17
00:00:24,208 --> 00:00:25,442
are why it never sinks!
